//!
//! # Trap
//!
//! How the processor enters the kernel after the assembly stubs have saved its
//! state: the interrupt dispatcher and the CPU exception handling.
//!
//! ## Public API
//!
//! | Name              | File            | Purpose                                                  |
//! |-------------------|-----------------|----------------------------------------------------------|
//! | `Trap::dispatch`  | `dispatch.ign`  | called by `interrupt_asm.S` for every vector             |
//! | `Trap::KEYBOARD_VECTOR`, `Trap::TIMER_VECTOR` | `dispatch.ign` | the two device vectors the kernel uses |
//! | `Trap::Exception` | `exception.ign` | exception names, the fatal report, killing a faulting process |
//! | `Trap::Setup`     | `setup.ign`     | GDT, IDT and `SYSCALL` setup, with their boot log lines  |
//!
//! ## Dependencies
//!
//! | Imports   | Why                                                                |
//! |-----------|--------------------------------------------------------------------|
//! | `Arch`    | the 8259, the GDT, the IDT, `Arch::Cpu::haltForever`, `Arch::InterruptFrame` |
//! | `Apic`    | the end-of-interrupt write and the spurious vector                 |
//! | `Drivers` | the PS/2 interrupt handler and the exception report                |
//! | `Time`    | `Time::Timer::handleTick` on every timer interrupt                 |
//! | `Sched`   | `Sched::Scheduler::onTick` may switch threads                      |
//! | `Proc`    | a fault in ring 3 kills the current process                        |
//!
//! `Trap` sits near the top of the dependency order because the dispatcher
//! reaches into the drivers, the clock, the scheduler and the processes. It
//! would be part of `Arch` if `Arch` could import them, but `Arch` is a leaf.
//! Only `main` and `Tests` import `Trap`.
//!
//! The assembly stub calls `dispatch` by its `@externName` symbol, so this
//! facade has to be imported or the dispatcher is never compiled.

import _ from "./dispatch";
import _ from "./exception";
import _ from "./setup";

/// Aggregate namespace of the trap code. `dispatch.ign` adds the dispatcher
/// and the vector numbers, `exception.ign` adds `Trap::Exception` and
/// `setup.ign` adds `Trap::Setup`.
export namespace Trap {}
